\f5 \cf8 \cb9 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \CocoaLigature0 \outl0\strokewidth0 Five decisions you need to make. I'll mark my recommendation for each:                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                       \
  
\f6\b \cf16 \cb9 a) Parameter name(s) we accept
\f5\b0 \cf8 \cb9                                                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                       \
  - 
\f6\b \cf16 \cb9 (i)
\f5\b0 \cf8 \cb9  Accept both \cf10 ?shConId=X&shColId=Y\cf8  AND \cf10 ?shN=X&shL=Y\cf8                                                                                 \
  - 
\f6\b \cf16 \cb9 (ii)
\f5\b0 \cf8 \cb9  Only one canonical set\
                                                                                                                                         \
  
\f6\b \cf16 \cb9 Recommendation: (i)
\f5\b0 \cf8 \cb9  \'97 partners are likely to send BC-native names (\cf10 shConId\cf8 /\cf10 shColId\cf8 ) since those are the underlying identifiers; we     \
  accept either.                                                                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                         \
  
\f6\b \cf16 \cb9 b) Where the redirect fires
\f5\b0 \cf8 \cb9                                                                                                           \
\
  - 
\f6\b \cf16 \cb9 (i)
\f5\b0 \cf8 \cb9  Client-side in \cf10 App.js\cf8  (on mount, check URL \uc0\u8594  consult registry \u8594  \cf10 navigate()\cf8 )                                                      \
  - 
\f6\b \cf16 \cb9 (ii)
\f5\b0 \cf8 \cb9  Server-side in BC's VPS nginx (pre-React)\
                                                                                                                                         \
  
\f6\b \cf16 \cb9 Recommendation: (i) client-side.
\f5\b0 \cf8 \cb9  Reasons: works without BC changes, easier to A/B test, the bundle owns its own routing decisions. The \
  cost is one extra render before redirect \'97 usually invisible.\
                                                                                                                                         \
  
\f6\b \cf16 \cb9 c) Lookup key \'97 what gets matched in the registry
\f5\b0 \cf8 \cb9                                                                                       \
  \
  - 
\f6\b \cf16 \cb9 (i)
\f5\b0 \cf8 \cb9  Exact: \cf10 "<shConId>:<shColId>"\cf8                                                                                                      \
  - 
\f6\b \cf16 \cb9 (ii)
\f5\b0 \cf8 \cb9  Fallback chain: try exact \uc0\u8594  fall back to \cf10 "<shConId>:*"\cf8  \uc0\u8594  fall back to \cf10 "*:<shColId>"\cf8  \uc0\u8594  fall back to \cf10 "default"\cf8                   \
  - 
\f6\b \cf16 \cb9 (iii)
\f5\b0 \cf8 \cb9  Just exact, no fallback \'97 unknown combo = default config                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                         \
  
\f6\b \cf16 \cb9 Recommendation: (ii) fallback chain.
\f5\b0 \cf8 \cb9  Lets you define partner-wide defaults (every page from Partner A gets the same UX unless          \
  overridden) AND page-wide variants (every partner hitting Page X gets a specific variant). Powerful with low complexity.               \
                                                                                                                                         \
  
\f6\b \cf16 \cb9 d) Persistence and URL hygiene
\f5\b0 \cf8 \cb9                                                                                                        \
\
  - 
\f6\b \cf16 \cb9 (i)
\f5\b0 \cf8 \cb9  Strip \cf10 shConId\cf8 /\cf10 shColId\cf8  from URL after capture (URL ends up clean: \cf10 /name/landing/v5\cf8 )                                               \
  - 
\f6\b \cf16 \cb9 (ii)
\f5\b0 \cf8 \cb9  Keep them in URL (URL stays \cf10 /name/landing/v5?shConId=X&shColId=Y\cf8 )\
                                                                                                                                         \
  
\f6\b \cf16 \cb9 Recommendation: (i) strip them.
\f5\b0 \cf8 \cb9  Cleaner shareable URLs; sessionStorage holds the values; SEO doesn't care. Existing GTM                \
  \cf10 captureReferralParams\cf8  already follows this pattern.                                                                                    \
                                                                                                                                         \
  
\f6\b \cf16 \cb9 e) What happens if shConId+shColId combo is unknown
\f5\b0 \cf8 \cb9                                                                                     \
  \
  - 
\f6\b \cf16 \cb9 (i)
